  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '

    Welcome to the documentation of the terminal!


    you can use
    the terminal to compile code and solve glithced items in order to fix the world.



    <color=#c2c2c2><b>Table
    of Contents</b>

    <i>1.compilation</i>

    <i>2.conditions</i>

    <i>3.errors</i>

    <i>4.restore</i>

    <i>5.hint</i>

    </color>



    <i>1.
    compilation</i>


    you can run code using the <color=black>Run code</color>
    from the console.


    the code automatically <color=blue>saves</color> when
    running sucessfully.


    your code will not run if it does not pass the conditions.



    <i>2.conditions</i>


    your
    edited code must adheere to the conditions written in <color=#031700>/* comments
    */</color> at the bottom of every terminal.


    be sure to read all conditions
    carefully!



    <i>3.errors</i>


    if you modify any original code you will
    receive the "<color=red>Compiler error!</color>" message.


    if your modified
    code doesn''t respect the conditions you will receive the "<color=red>Validation
    error!</color>" message.



    <i>4.restore</i>


    you can use the <color=black>restore</color>
    button on the top left to restore you code to the last <color=blue>saved</color>
    version.


    this can be useful if you change any original code and don''t
    know what used to be there.



    <i>5.hint</i>


    the <color=purple>hint</color>
    button on the top left can be used to aid you when struggling to solve any puzzle.
    use it at your disgression!



    thank you for playing!



'
